    "result_text": "The only external caller, `OwnerMapper.identityKey`, uses `IdentityKey.forOwner(owner)`, whose signature is unchanged \u2014 so it transparently gets the new hashed key on the response.\n\nThe change is complete and the full suite is green. Here's what I did:\n\n## Summary\n\nRedesigned the owner identity key to `identityKey = SHA-256 hex over (normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName))`, and moved duplicate detection onto that single key.\n\n**New file**\n- `util/Soundex.java` \u2014 a pure American Soundex helper (first letter + three digits), reused by both the identity key and the soft-match. Placed alongside the existing `Sha256` util.\n\n**Identity key** (`IdentityKey.java`)\n- `of(...)` now hashes with `Sha256.hex` and its third component is `Soundex.of(lastName)` instead of the household id; `forOwner` passes `owner.getLastName()`. Produces the 64-char lower-case hex the spec/tests require.\n\n**Duplicate detection / 409** (`EnsureUniqueIdentity.java`)\n- Now rejects when an existing **active** owner has the same identity key. Deleted owners are still ignored; the email-domain blocklist still runs earlier in the pipeline (`ValidateEmailDomain`) so it's applied first. Two owners with the same last name + postcode but different telephones now have different keys \u2192 no 409.\n\n**Soft match** (`FlagPossibleDuplicate.java`)\n- Now flags a possible duplicate when the identity key **differs** but `soundex(lastName)` and postcode match (the household-member-with-a-different-phone case), recording the earliest matching owner. The `sharesHousehold` opt-out is preserved.\n\n**Supporting**\n- `DuplicateIdentityException` now carries the identity key (message/field/getter renamed accordingly; the 409 handler is unchanged).\n- Removed the now-defunct household-based 409 block, and updated the `HouseholdNormalizer` javadoc \u2014 the household id now feeds only `CountHousehold`/`CapMembershipLevel`, while duplicate detection and the soft flag key off `IdentityKey`.\n\nTests: `AcceptanceTest` (SHA-256 hex shape + identical-identity 409) and the full suite \u2014 **11 run, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS**.",
